# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env.example — safe template committed to version control
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values.
# NEVER commit .env / .env.local / .env.production — they are in .gitignore.
#
# This portfolio is fully static — no runtime secrets are required right now.
# Add variables here when integrating a backend (e.g. a contact form API route).
#
# Vercel-specific env vars are managed in the Vercel Dashboard:
#   Project → Settings → Environment Variables
# They are injected at build time and NEVER stored in this repository.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Example: contact form API endpoint (if you add a serverless function later)
# VITE_CONTACT_API_URL=https://your-api.vercel.app/api/contact

# Example: analytics write key (safe — client-side only)
# VITE_ANALYTICS_ID=your_public_write_key
